  [PASS] LIM-0  the CAM kernel mu(y) = Q'(y)/(2y) = 1 - e^{-y} -> 1 as y -> infinity (high acceleration): the constitutive law Newtonises exponentially   (mu(y)=1-e^{-y} -> 1 as y->inf)

==============================================================================================================
PART 1 -- the CAM Poisson equation (mu Phi')' = rho/4M^2 -> Phi'' = rho/4M^2 (Newton) as mu->1.
