==============================================================================================================
  [PASS] BETA-1  as mu -> 1 the CAM field equation is LINEAR (standard Poisson), so gravitational potentials superpose with no anomalous nonlinear term -- the PPN nonlinearity parameter beta = 1, as in GR; any deviation is O(e^{-g/a0})   (linear Poisson (mu->1) => no anomalous Phi^2 potential => beta = 1 (GR), deviation O(e^{-g/a0}))

